  "problem_statement": "Add a nanocoap API function coap_iterate_uri_query that lets a caller iterate through the URI query options of a CoAP packet one option at a time. The caller supplies a context pointer, buffers for the key and value, and the sizes of those buffers. The first call is made with the context initialized to NULL; each call updates the context for the next option. URI query options are expected to use the key=value convention, and an option with only a key is treated as a key whose value is empty. The function copies the key and value into the supplied buffers as null-terminated strings. It returns 2 when a value is present, 1 when only a key is present, 0 when no more options are found, and -E2BIG when the key or value does not fit the supplied buffer size. Repeated calls from the same context must yield all URI query options in order, for example foo=bar&baz=blub yields foo/bar, then baz/blub, then 0.",
